[center][size=6][b]KOTOR, played together.[/b][/size]
[size=4]Your own character. A shared adventure. A friend beside you.[/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/nexus/images/1-cover-title.jpg[/img]

[url=https://github.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/releases/latest]Latest release[/url]  |  [url=https://christophervr.github.io/kotor-coop/#trailer]Watch the trailer[/url]  |  [url=https://christophervr.github.io/kotor-coop/]Player guides[/url][/center]

A free, open-source co-op mod for [b]Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic[/b]. One player hosts; friends join the same world from their own copies of the game. Explore, fight and share the story through the original game's menus, with a new [b]Co-op[/b] button to bring you together.

[b][color=#ff9900]EXPERIMENTAL BETA — start with two players and back up your saves.[/color][/b]
Selected scenes have been tested on real game copies. A complete co-op campaign has not been verified. Up to eight players can connect, but larger-group campaign reliability remains experimental.

Real game footage, recorded using [b]two game copies on one PC[/b] and disposable saves. The menu, character, inventory, chat and reconnect clips were captured on [b]v0.1.0-beta.4[/b] using the background game harness. Cuts are labeled. The exploration, dialogue and combat clips come from our earlier gameplay trailer.

[size=5][b]Host from the game menu[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/site/media/showcase/host-from-menu.gif[/img]
[i]Open Co-op, choose Host, then enter Dantooine after loading.[/i][/center]

Start a session from [b]Co-op → Host[/b]. Shown here: hosting an existing save in the Jedi Enclave. The loading wait is cut from the loop. [url=https://christophervr.github.io/kotor-coop/media/showcase/host-from-menu.mp4]Watch or pause this clip.[/url]

[size=5][b]Create your own character[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/site/media/showcase/create-character.gif[/img]
[i]The joining player chooses a Soldier and cycles through portraits.[/i][/center]

A first-time join opens the game's character creator. Shown here: class and portrait choices for the new Soldier who joined this session. The clip cuts between those steps. [url=https://christophervr.github.io/kotor-coop/media/showcase/create-character.mp4]Watch or pause this clip.[/url]

[size=5][b]Explore together[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/site/media/showcase/explore-together.gif[/img]
[i]Two connected players moving through Korriban, shown from both game copies.[/i][/center]

See your friend as a character in the world. Walk together, follow each other through area changes and take the same trip between planets. Each player has their own character, backpack and credits.

[size=5][b]Share the conversation[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/site/media/showcase/share-conversations.gif[/img]
[i]One player speaks to Belaya; the other selects her and joins the conversation on Dantooine.[/i][/center]

Whoever starts a conversation chooses the replies. The other player selects the same character to watch; story-triggered scenes bring the party in automatically. [b]One conversation runs at a time.[/b] Quest items and journal progress are shared so the story can move forward together.

[size=5][b]Fight side by side[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/site/media/showcase/fight-together.gif[/img]
[i]Blue and yellow sabers against the same kath hounds on Dantooine.[/i][/center]

Fight shared enemies with your own character and gear. Enemies scale for a group; playing alone leaves that scaling off.

[size=5][b]Your character. Your gear.[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/site/media/showcase/personal-inventory.gif[/img]
[i]Both players open their own inventories and character sheets.[/i][/center]

Open your backpack and character sheet independently. Shown here: the established host has gear, while the newly created Soldier has an empty backpack and his own stats. [url=https://christophervr.github.io/kotor-coop/media/showcase/personal-inventory.mp4]Watch or pause this clip.[/url]

[size=5][b]Keep talking while you explore[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ChristopherVR/kotor-coop/main/site/media/showcase/in-game-chat.gif[/img]
